 metrics stabilize."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-08-31 filing) that could show whether FCF/working capital dynamics are normalizing.","Continued capital rotation into the Technology sector.","Potential conversion of elevated inventory/working capital into realized sales and cash flow if AI-server demand materializes as implied by revenue growth."],"risks":["FCF is deeply negative (-17.8% margin, -555% growth) with OCF of -6.8B, raising sustainability concerns if working capital needs persist.","Share count rose 11% YoY, diluting per-share value creation despite strong net income growth.","Gross margin is thin (10.8%), leaving limited cushion if component costs rise or pricing competition intensifies.","Macro regime is split nearly evenly across Goldilocks/Reflation/Stagflation/Contraction (27.7/22.4/22.3/27.6), meaning no clear macro tailwind is guaranteed."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 54% (currently 77.8%).","ROIC falls below 41% (currently 55.0%).","Operating margin YoY change falls below -2.0 pts (currently +1.4 pts).","Technology rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (currently +68).","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently 49.9% combined).","Price closes more than 10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Component suppliers (GPU, memory, storage vendors) that benefit from Supermicro's accelerating revenue and server shipment volumes.","Contract manufacturers and logistics/supply-chain partners that help manage the elevated inventory and working-capital build implied by the negative FCF.","Lenders or trade-finance/factoring providers who could extend working-capital financing to bridge the cash-flow gap while revenue growth continues.","Thermal/cooling and power-infrastructure suppliers tied to high-density server deployments, if the revenue acceleration reflects AI-server demand."],"ep